// A function value is never an element of a list (docs/SPEC.md 1.1). A list is
// data that travels, and a function value inside one could be called anywhere
// the list reaches, with no function type written at the call. So an element
// that is one is refused as that, rather than as an element of the wrong type.

fv_typed(int e) {
  string t = type_of(e);
  int ok = ty_is_func(t);
} return int ok;
